member.summary:
Read-only assets shipped inside the app package. On desktop this is {DataPath}/Content;
the build pipeline copies loose files / paks / bundles here. On Android it conceptually maps
to the APK's assets/ VFS (the Android host translates this path).

            A writable directory that survives app updates and is backed up by the OS. Per-OS convention:


Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\{CompanyName}\{ProductName}

macOS: ~/Library/Application Support/{CompanyName}/{ProductName}

iOS: the app Documents folder

Linux: ~/.local/share/{CompanyName}/{ProductName}

            Used for downloaded bundle updates (SandboxBundleStore) and per-player save data.

Direct dependency  for an asset (its own bundle plus any
            extra DependentBundleIds). Does NOT include transitive bundle dependencies of those bundles;
            use  / the AssetBundleManifest wrapper for closure.

Package-facing declaration for a component that uses the Graphic on its GameObject to write
an entry into the Canvas stencil buffer. The Runtime host owns traversal and GPU submission;
packages implement this interface without making the host depend on their concrete type.

remarks.para:
On a property: the property's current value is drawn. Properties are never serialized;
this attribute is display-only. Set  to draw the value as read-only
(recommended for computed properties that have no setter or whose setter has side effects).

member.summary:
             Records a sequence of GPU commands without touching the GL context. Submit the
             buffer through  to enqueue it for the render thread.
             Buffers are pooled; the typical pattern is:


               using var cmd = Graphics.GetCommandBuffer("My Pass");
               cmd.SetRenderTarget(rt);
               cmd.ClearRenderTarget(ClearFlags.Color | ClearFlags.Depth, Color.Black);
               cmd.DrawMesh(mesh, material);
               Graphics.Submit(cmd);



Single-producer: only one thread encodes a given buffer. CBs execute on the
             render thread in submit order, so an upload CB can be safely followed by a CB
             that uses the uploaded data.


, , and
              all snapshot the PropertyState at encode
             time, so the caller is free to mutate the original immediately after.

While true, every raster state recorded via  is forced
            to wireframe fill — the editor's Wireframe debug view. Scene-geometry passes toggle it on;
            grid/UI/post passes record with it off. Callers reset it after their draw block.

When true, the attachment binds a single cubemap face (selected by
            ) instead of a 2D texture. Used for rendering into a
            reflection-probe cubemap face.

Stable, low-cardinality device facts used to select Android render tiers and to make
device evidence reproducible. The collection is populated once during device creation;
it is not intended for per-frame feature probing.

CPU projection helpers for light cookies. Directional uses an ortho slab along the
light's travel direction; spots use the same perspective cone as spot shadows;
points use a lat-long mapping of the light-to-fragment direction.

Spatial / temporal upscaler (U17-M3). STP reuses the existing TAA history path;
FSR is recorded as a spatial filter (bilinear until an FSR shader lands). Auto
picks Linear at native scale and STP when TAA or STP is requested.

Ear-clipping triangulation of a simple polygon. Appends triangle indices (into )
to  and returns false if the polygon is degenerate. Holes aren't handled;
a hole loop just triangulates as a solid, which is harmless since its texels are transparent.

member.remarks:
Created by  during asset
import. Treat as read-only once imported to change it, edit the parent asset's importer
settings and reimport.

Volume sampling (GPU shader):
  uvw = (localPos - Bounds.Min) / (Bounds.Max - Bounds.Min);
  distance = texture(volume, uvw).r;

member.summary:
Fraction of the mesh bounds extent a single level-0 collapse may deviate;
            the budget doubles each level as legitimate LOD deviation grows. Candidates beyond it
            are dropped so the mesh under-simplifies instead of baking a wild error.

Registers a serialized type-name redirect without retaining a  from a
package load context. The alias is normalized to the type name plus simple assembly name,
so old Echo data that includes version/culture metadata resolves identically.

★ M40 — Bind-time resolution of authored  to zero-arg
 slots. Reflection and delegate allocation happen here (cold);
per-frame fire is an indexed invoke.

Advances the playhead by  seconds (scaled by
), applying the configured  mode when bounded.
Returns the scaled delta actually applied.

Hot-reload: detach script-bound continuations from every bridge source that is still waiting
on a BCL Task. The Task itself cannot be reached, so the source's awaiter is dropped instead;
a late Task completion lands on the detached source harmlessly.

